{"id":"F054","verdict":"accept","strength":"medium","label":"1B","direction":"supports","note":"Verified: 10B-300 non-profit $2,234 (Aug 2023 and Mar 2024) → $1,765.67 external (1 Jul 2026), −21%. 25B-300 $3,538 → $3,512.47. Using Illumina's output specs (10B-300 ~3 Tb / 8 lanes = 375 Gb; 25B-300 ~8 Tb / 8 lanes = 1 Tb, ratio 0.375, not 0.4), the 10B per-Gb premium falls from ~68% to ~34%. UCLA marks X lanes as 'material pass-through at cost', so this tracks UCLA's purchase price. It largely quantifies the known 'harmonised cost per read across 5B/10B/25B' (late 2025), so it is incremental rather than novel. The 2026 page shows only one external column, which matches the old non-profit tier."},
{"id":"F055","verdict":"accept","strength":"medium","label":"1B","direction":"against","note":"Verified: 25B-300 $3,168 internal / $3,538 non-profit / $3,933 profit in both the Aug 2023 and Mar 2024 sheets; $3,512.47 external on the 1 Jul 2026 page. The footnote says X lanes are 'Material Pass Through rates… at cost', which makes this a better proxy for UCLA's Illumina purchase price than a policy rate. Prep rises verified: mRNA $63 → $68.14, DNA $61 → $68.90. Consistent with the known Harvard +17.8% FY27 move. List-anchored pass-through at a mid-size core; large-account net prices could still diverge."},
